{"base_rate":0.5852047556142669,"brier":0.18532324966974897,"bss":0.2365364775488492,"bss_hi":0.34781034607666067,"bss_lo":0.12482292025925254,"country":"GB","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13404227212681638,"ess":379.281183938315,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Preston</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Preston rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>87%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>16%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nPRESTON: MOOR PARK, 1.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.24, ranked 82 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(48&ndash;100) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>140</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>31%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>66%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>87%</b></td><td class='num'>309</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Preston</b> <span class=\"muted\">GB</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.24</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>48&ndash;100\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Preston &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Preston\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.101142857142854,379.4 78.66475,341.05 164.023,236.4 278.95116883116884,117.27272727272725 353.7645070422535,48.76056338028167 408.2881553398058,18.0 408.2881553398058,26.24595469255661 353.7645070422535,110.28169014084506 278.95116883116884,192.90909090909093 164.023,309.2 78.66475,377.45 58.101142857142854,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"168.98546895640686\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"168.98546895640686\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.101142857142854,322.2 78.66475,268.25 164.023,236.4 278.95116883116884,159.8181818181818 353.7645070422535,141.04225352112675 408.2881553398058,65.11974110032361\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 140 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.101142857142854\" cy=\"322.2\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 31% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"78.66475\" cy=\"268.25\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 30%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"164.023\" cy=\"236.4\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 62%&amp;#10;It rained 61% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"278.95116883116884\" cy=\"159.8181818181818\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 66% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"353.7645070422535\" cy=\"141.04225352112675\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 87% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 309 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"408.2881553398058\" cy=\"65.11974110032361\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(59%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Preston the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.48) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.12).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'>-0.119</td><td class='num'>19.3%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'>0.101</td><td class='num'>16.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'>0.205</td><td class='num'>14.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.484</td><td class='num'>8.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":53.76282,"lon":-2.70452,"n":757,"n_cities":109,"name":"Preston","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00028571428571428574,"n":140,"obs":0.16428571428571428,"sig":true},{"hi":0.16,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.058374999999999996,"n":80,"obs":0.3125,"sig":true},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.16,"mean":0.2995,"n":80,"obs":0.4,"sig":false},{"hi":0.76,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.6241558441558441,"n":77,"obs":0.6103896103896104,"sig":false},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.76,"mean":0.8354929577464789,"n":71,"obs":0.6619718309859155,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9895145631067961,"n":309,"obs":0.8705501618122977,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.2,"rank":82,"rank_hi":100.0,"rank_lo":48.0,"reliability":0.02148655895781785,"resolution":0.07810349532841351,"slug":"preston","station":"PRESTON: MOOR PARK","timezone":"Europe/London"}